  "uprn": "100021560538",
  "decision_date": "09/09/2004",
  "description": "Conversion of dwellinghouse into 2 x one -bedroom flats and 2 x two-bedroom flats",
  "site_name": "33",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "17/05/2004",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": null,
  "street_name": "St Stephens Road",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major all other major developments",
  "lapsed_date": "08/09/2009",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - It is considered that the conversion of existing property to provide two one-bedroom flats and two two-bedroom flats, would be acceptable having due regard for the site characteristics of 33 St Stephen's Road. The proposal accords with the Councils Residential Standards and Controls, would not be detrimental to the amenities of the adjoining and neighbouring properties, would preserve the character of St Stephen's Conservation Area and would not result in conditions prejudicial to the free flow of traffic or pedestrian and highway safety. The proposal is therefore in accordance with Unitary Development Plan (December 2003) policies ENV-B.1.1, ENV-B 2.2, H.3.4, H 4.1, H.4.2 and T.1.4.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be completed within 6 months of the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is occupied.",
    "Condition : 4 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of  08.00 to 18.00 on Mondays to Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and public holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 5 - No development shall take place until full details of both hard and soft landscape works have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority and these works shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given and shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied. These details shall include means of enclosure (including the division of the rear garden to provide separate private amenity space for each flat); car parking layouts; other vehicle and pedestrian access and circulation areas and hard surfacing material. Soft landscape works shall include planting plans, noting species, plant sizes and proposed numbers/densities where appropriate.",
    "Condition : 6 - A splay of 2.4m x 2.4m shall be provided on each side of the access, the depth measured from the back of the footway and the widths outwards from the edges of the access, and no fence, wall or other obstruction to visibility exceeding 0.6m in height above the surface of the adjoining highway shall be erected within the areas of such splays.",
    "Condition : 7 - The use hereby permitted shall not be begun until details of the arrangements for storing of waste and recycled materials have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The arrangements for storing waste and recycled materials shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given and shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 8 - The newly created dwellings shall not be occupied until it has been demonstated to the satisfaction of the Local Planning Authority that the construction of the internal walls, floors and other building elements meet the requirements of the Building Regulations 2000, Approved document E- Resistance to the passage of sound (2003 Edition)"
  ],
